## Critical Path Analysis

### Mandatory Sequencing (Hard Blockers)

| Step | Must Complete Before | Reason |
|:---|:---|:---|
| **A.1** (Redis container up) | **A.1.3** (rate-limit.ts refactor) | Changing URL to 6380 before container exists crashes intake |
| **A.2** (auth-guard.ts + migration 029) | **A.5** (login fix) | Login fix removes old auth flow, needs new guard utilities available |
| **A.2** (auth-guard.ts) | **A.7** (protected layouts) | Layouts call `requireUser/requireRole/requirePrivileged` |
| **A.2** (auth-guard.ts) | **A.8** (API route auth) | Routes call `requireRole` |
| **A.2** (auth-guard.ts) | **A.9** (service-role removal) | `org-dashboard` uses `createAuthenticatedClient()` from guard |
| **A.6** (SSO env vars) | **A.5** (login PKCE fix) | Login page needs `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` env var before changing redirectTo |
| **A.4** (remove `useCrdtStore`) | **B.3** (`resolveComplaint`) | `columns.tsx` must be free of CRDT import before Server Action wiring |
| **A.2** (`requireUser()` pattern) | **B.3** (`resolveComplaint`) | Resolve action calls `requireUser()` |
| **A.3 + A.4** (OTEL + offline removed) | **Final build** | Partial removal breaks the build |

### Parallelizable Work (No Dependencies)

```
Group 1 (independent):      A.1 → A.1.3 → A.1.4
Group 2 (independent):      A.2 (auth-guard + migration + JWT)
Group 3 (independent):      A.3 (all OTEL removal)
Group 4 (after A.3):        A.4 (offline removal)
Group 5 (after A.2):        A.6 → A.5 (SSO env → login fix)
Group 6 (after A.2):        A.7 (protected layouts)
Group 7 (after A.2):        A.8 (API route auth)
Group 8 (after A.2 + A.7):  A.9 (service-role removal — layout protects page)
Group 9 (anytime):          B.1, B.2 (database only — no code deps on each other)
Group 10 (after A.4 + A.2): B.3 (resolve action)
Group 11 (anytime):         C.1, C.2 (no code deps)
```

### Recommended Execution Order

```
 1. A.2    — Create auth-guard.ts + migration 029 + JWT_EXPIRY    [FOUNDATION — unblocks 5 tasks]
 2. A.1    — Stand up Redis container                              [independent]
 3. A.1.3  — Refactor rate-limit.ts                                [depends on A.1]
 4. A.6    — SSO config to env vars                                [unblocks A.5]
 5. A.5    — Fix login cookie synthesis → PKCE                     [depends on A.2, A.6]
 6. A.7    — Create protected layouts                              [depends on A.2]
 7. A.8    — Secure unprotected API routes                         [depends on A.2]
 8. A.9    — Remove service-role from render paths                 [depends on A.2, A.7]
 9. A.3    — Strip all OTEL (atomic batch)                         [independent]
10. A.4    — Remove all offline-sync (atomic batch)                [independent]
11. Wire auth-guard into refactored Server Actions (A.2.5–A.2.8)  [depends on A.2, A.3]
12. B.1    — Run migration 030: drop FK                            [independent]
13. B.2    — Run migration 031: add key_version                    [independent]
14. B.3    — Build resolveComplaint + wire Resolve button          [depends on A.4, A.2]
15. C.1    — Verify mock OTP
16. C.2    — Create aws-secrets scaffold + .env.example
17. FINAL  — pnpm install → pnpm build → E2E verification
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **A.2 (auth-guard.ts) is the critical path bottleneck.** It must be built first because 5 downstream tasks (A.5, A.7, A.8, A.9, B.3) depend on it. Prioritize this above all else.

